            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-amber-400 mb-4">Top 10 Best Items to Flip in Deadman Mode</h1>
            <p class="text-gray-400">Updated: February 2026 • 4 min read</p>
        </header>

        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 mb-8">
            We've analyzed millions of GE transactions from previous DMM seasons. 
            Here is the definitive list of top 10 items that offer the best balance of volume, margin, and risk.
        </p>

        <h2>Tier 1: Safe & Consistent (The "Bread and Butter")</h2>
        
        <h3>1. Sharks / Mantas</h3>
        <p>
            Food is the fuel of DMM. Every PKer needs it. Margins are tight (50-100gp), but you can flip thousands per hour. 
            Always buy raw if you have the cooking level, or flip cooked for pure volume.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Super Restores (4)</h3>
        <p>
            More valuable than Prayer Potions because of the stat drain mechanics in DMM (brews drain stats). 
            Look for margins of 300-600gp per potion.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Death Runes & Blood Runes</h3>
        <p>
            Ancient Magicks (Ice Barrage) is the meta. These runes never stop selling. 
            Buy overnight when NA/EU sleeps and sell during peak hours.
        </p>

        <h2>Tier 2: PK Gear (The "Lost and Found")</h2>

        <h3>4. Mystic Robe Sets</h3>
        <p>
            The standard PK outfit. Players die in these daily, meaning they buy new sets daily. 
            Flipping individual pieces (Top/Bottom) often has better margins than sets.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Black D'hide Body</h3>
        <p>
            Cheap, effective, and constantly lost. A staple item with very consistent margins.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Rune Crossbow</h3>
        <p>
            The entry-level weapon for every ranger. Pay attention to the price of Runite Limbs as well—sometimes you can profit by fletching them.
        </p>

        <h3>7. Dragon Dagger (p++)</h3>
        <p>
            The most popular spec weapon. Nearly every account has one. 
            Buy unpoisoned ones and poison them yourself for extra profit.
        </p>

        <h2>Tier 3: High Ticket (The "Jackpot")</h2>

        <h3>8. Amulet of Glory (4) / (6)</h3>
        <p>
            Teleportation is survival. Charged glories command a premium. 
            Buy uncharged, charge them at the Fountain of Rune (risky!) or Heroes' Guild, and sell for massive profit.
        </p>

        <h3>9. Ancient Staff</h3>
        <p>
            Required for Ancients. Supply is limited to drops or shops (Desert Treasure). 
            Deep margin potential during the first week.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Granite Maul</h3>
        <p>
            The combo weapon of choice. When pures are active, this item flies. 
            Also keep an eye on the Handle attachment price.
        </p>

